# AIDE HANDOFF

Cold-start protocol for agents reorienting on this project. This is a
snapshot of the current architectural intent, the implementation gap
between intent and code, and the pipeline phase that comes next. It is
NOT historical commentary — superseded design decisions are cut, not
annotated.

---

## Cold-start protocol (do this first if you're picking up cold)

**The brain layer is fully aligned at every level.** Intent, plans,
code, tests, and the agent-readable surface (orchestrator prompt,
brain config skill) are all coherent across the cascading tree.
Three multi-module cycles are complete: (1) the brain.aide schema
collapse, (2) hub-artifact sourcing from brain.aide body sections,
and (3) the agent-invokes-sync wiring loop that closes the broken-
state recovery flow without any terminal context-switching.
`aide_discover` reports no `status: misaligned` anywhere under
`src/service/`.

**What just landed (this most recent cycle):** the brain config flow
no longer punts the user to a terminal for `npx aidemd-mcp sync`. The
canonical orchestrator command (`.claude/commands/aide.md`) and the
brain config skill (`.claude/commands/aide/brain.md`) were both
rewritten so the agent invokes sync via Bash on the user's behalf.
All three broken-state branches (`no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`,
`mcp-drift`) now route uniformly: orchestrator delegates to the brain
config skill; the skill detects which state, scaffolds via
`aide_init` when needed (no-brain-aide only), then runs sync via Bash
by recovering the launcher from `.mcp.json["mcpServers"]["aide"]`,
then asks the user to restart Claude Code as the single remaining
manual step. The same cycle swept retired vocabulary that was leaking
into agent prose: the `invalid-path` boot state branch (retired with
`rootPath` in the schema collapse) is gone from the orchestrator,
and `rootPath` references in the README and orchestrator are gone.
Verified end-to-end via integration test in `D:/Code/Me/aide-fresh`
against all three broken states — agent successfully ran sync via
Bash on each, no terminal context-switching required.

**The cycle before that** (commits `1fa1d3e`, `888df56`, `ed84d94`)
was the brain.aide schema collapse: hub-artifact bytes flow from
brain.aide body sections via `parseBrainAide` rather than inline
TypeScript constants; the `## Prose`-only body grew to three sections
(`## Prose`, `## Playbook hub`, `## Research hub`); the vault-root
`CLAUDE.md` scaffold was retired entirely; the framework's brain
contract is now exactly two required hubs (coding-playbook + research);
storage-specific identifiers in `provisionBrain/index.ts` were swept
(`vaultExists` → `brainRootExists`, `VAULT_DIRS` → `BRAIN_ROOT_DIRS`,
etc.). The `obsidian` token remains only where it names content
(the `obsidianBrainAideTemplate` helper folder, the `.obsidian`
directory heuristic comment) or the legacy MCP key being migrated
away from.

**Tests: 824/824 passing. tsc: clean.**

If you're picking up cold, the next pipeline phase is whatever the
user wants — there's no in-flight build work waiting to land. The
followup items below are independent, not blockers.

