## The implementation gap (what the code does NOT yet do)

Everything in the brain layer's runtime, intent tree, agent skill
prompts, and orchestrator is aligned. The remaining gap items are
small followups, not blockers:

| Item | Current state | Needed |
|---|---|---|
| `.aide/docs/brain-aide.md` | Documents the 2-field frontmatter and the single `## Prose` body section. | Update the body section to document the 3-section body schema (`## Prose`, `## Playbook hub`, `## Research hub`), the closed-vocabulary parser rule, and the per-consumer ownership pattern. |
| `src/cli/sync/index.ts` IIFE | Top-level auto-exec calls `process.exit(1)` on error during module import, which vitest surfaces as an "Error: 1 error" line during test runs. All tests still pass; the noise is purely test-harness teardown. | Extract the body of the IIFE into an exported function and gate the auto-exec on an `import.meta.main`-style check (or equivalent) so importing the module for testing doesn't trigger business logic. Small structural refactor; not blocking. |
| `src/index.ts` MCP tool descriptions | The advertised schemas for `aide_info`, `aide_brain`, and `aide_init` describe the pre-collapse API. `aide_info`'s description names a three-state union (`ok` / `no-mcp-entry` / `invalid-path`) and a `vaultPath` field that don't exist on `BrainState`. `aide_brain`'s description names a `backend` field in the response that doesn't exist on `BrainToolResult`. `aide_init`'s description uses "vault path" terminology and a `brainPath` parameter description that conflict with the post-collapse `brain.aide`-as-source-of-truth model. The actual return types in `src/types/index.ts` are correct; only the advertised descriptions lie. | Sweep the descriptions to match the post-collapse types: `aide_info.brain.status` is one of four states (`ok`, `no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`), no `vaultPath`; `aide_brain` returns `{ status, instructions }` (no `backend`); `aide_init` describes brain wiring in terms of `brain.aide` as the source of truth. Higher-impact than it looks because the orchestrator and downstream agents read these descriptions at boot and pull terminology into their improvisations (the prior cycle's integration test caught the agent emitting "edit `rootPath`" advice that traced back to here). |
| `README.md` line ~225 (`aide_brain` reference section) | Still names `invalid-path` as one of the brain status values the tool can return. | Sweep to the four-state model. Same class as the `src/index.ts` cleanup; could be rolled into the same followup. |

